271
00:27:40,410 --> 00:27:43,520
Any ideas as to how we might change that state of affairs?

272
00:27:45,220 --> 00:27:46,150
Only one.

273
00:27:46,690 --> 00:27:47,940
Everyone stays here,

274
00:27:49,190 --> 00:27:50,770
and I go and talk to my sister.

275
00:27:52,470 --> 00:27:55,980
I didn't come all this way to have my Hand murdered.

276
00:27:55,980 --> 00:27:57,980
I don't want Cersei to murder me either.

277
00:27:57,980 --> 00:28:00,860
I could have stayed in my cell and saved a great deal of trouble.

278
00:28:01,040 --> 00:28:01,980
I did this.

279
00:28:03,290 --> 00:28:05,540
- I should go. - She'll definitely murder you.

280
00:28:06,180 --> 00:28:08,940
I go see my sister alone.

281
00:28:10,390 --> 00:28:11,510
Or we all go home

282
00:28:11,950 --> 00:28:13,600
and we're right back where we started.

283
00:29:15,620 --> 00:29:19,030
- You spoke with her? - At her until she kicked me out.

284
00:29:19,950 --> 00:29:22,730
She thinks I was an idiot to trust you.

285
00:29:23,120 --> 00:29:25,110
A lot of people seem to think that, actually.

286
00:29:25,110 --> 00:29:28,350
I'm about to step into a room with the most murderous woman

287
00:29:28,350 --> 00:29:32,110
in the world who's already tried to kill me twice, that I know of.

288
00:29:32,600 --> 00:29:33,670
Who's an idiot?

289
00:29:37,480 --> 00:29:39,450
I suppose we should say goodbye,

290
00:29:39,940 --> 00:29:41,450
one idiot to another.

291
00:30:40,450 --> 00:30:42,100
I shouldn't be surprised, I suppose.

292
00:30:42,100 --> 00:30:43,510
She's your kind of woman--

293
00:30:44,140 --> 00:30:46,210
a foreign whore who doesn't know her place.

294
00:30:46,860 --> 00:30:49,830
A foreign whore you can't abduct, beat, or intimidate.

295
00:30:50,770 --> 00:30:51,980
That must be difficult for you.

296
00:30:51,980 --> 00:30:53,490
So you bring her here with her pet Northerner,

297
00:30:53,490 --> 00:30:55,360
whom you've convinced to bow down before her.

298
00:30:55,360 --> 00:30:55,860
I didn't know about that.

299
00:30:55,870 --> 00:30:58,510
And now you've got them both working towards the same goal,

300
00:30:58,580 --> 00:31:00,540
the goal you've worked towards your entire life...

301
00:31:00,540 --> 00:31:03,100
- Cersei, I didn't know. - ...the destruction of this family.

302
00:31:04,360 --> 00:31:06,810
I am the one preventing that from happening.

303
00:31:07,340 --> 00:31:09,380
Daenerys didn't want to debate and negotiate.

304
00:31:09,380 --> 00:31:10,990
She didn't want to bring you words.

305
00:31:10,990 --> 00:31:12,990
She wanted to bring you fire and blood

306
00:31:13,110 --> 00:31:15,050
until I advised her otherwise.

307
00:31:15,050 --> 00:31:16,770
I don't want to destroy our family.

308
00:31:16,770 --> 00:31:18,170
I never have.

309
00:31:19,170 --> 00:31:20,330
You killed our father.

310
00:31:20,340 --> 00:31:21,840
After he sentenced me to death

311
00:31:21,840 --> 00:31:24,790
for a crime I didn't commit, yes, I killed him.

312
00:31:24,860 --> 00:31:26,230
Hate me for it if you want.

313
00:31:26,230 --> 00:31:28,610
I hate myself for it in spite of what he was,

314
00:31:28,610 --> 00:31:30,500
in spite of what he did to me.

315
00:31:30,500 --> 00:31:32,560
Oh, poor little man.

316
00:31:32,930 --> 00:31:34,630
Your papa was mean to you.

317
00:31:35,120 --> 00:31:38,410
Do you have any idea what you did when you fired that crossbow?

318
00:31:38,410 --> 00:31:39,740
You left us open.

319
00:31:40,620 --> 00:31:41,850
You laid us bare for the vultures,

320
00:31:41,850 --> 00:31:44,330
and the vultures came and tore us apart.

321
00:31:45,780 --> 00:31:47,060
You may not have killed Joffrey,

322
00:31:47,060 --> 00:31:49,110
but you killed Myrcella, you killed Tommen.

323
00:31:49,110 --> 00:31:50,860
No one would've touched them if Father was here.

324
00:31:50,860 --> 00:31:51,470
No one would have dared--

325
00:31:51,470 --> 00:31:53,610
I have never been more sorry about anything.

326
00:31:53,610 --> 00:31:55,300
I will not hear it, not from you.

327
00:31:55,300 --> 00:31:56,860
I will not hear it!

328
00:32:00,110 --> 00:32:01,110
All right.

329
00:32:02,520 --> 00:32:04,070
You love your family,

330
00:32:04,690 --> 00:32:06,400
and I have destroyed it.

331
00:32:07,090 --> 00:32:08,930
I will always be a threat.

332
00:32:09,610 --> 00:32:11,010
So put an end to me.

333
00:32:20,110 --> 00:32:22,190
If it weren't for me, you'd have a mother.

334
00:32:22,290 --> 00:32:24,880
If it weren't for me, you'd have a father.

335
00:32:24,880 --> 00:32:25,860
If it weren't for me,

336
00:32:25,860 --> 00:32:28,390
you'd have two beautiful children.

337
00:32:28,580 --> 00:32:30,390
I've thought about killing you

338
00:32:30,390 --> 00:32:32,530
more times than I can count.

339
00:32:33,810 --> 00:32:35,840
Do it! Say the word.

340
00:33:45,050 --> 00:33:48,160
I am more sorry about the children than you could ever know.

341
00:33:48,160 --> 00:33:50,860
- I will not-- - I don't care. I loved them.

342
00:33:51,360 --> 00:33:52,440
You know I did.

343
00:33:53,400 --> 00:33:56,770
You know it in your heart if there's anything left of it.

344
00:33:58,800 --> 00:33:59,750
It doesn't matter.

345
00:34:02,580 --> 00:34:05,500
Your love doesn't matter. Your feelings don't matter.

346
00:34:06,230 --> 00:34:08,120
I don't care why you did what you did.

347
00:34:08,120 --> 00:34:10,120
I only care what it cost us.

348
00:34:11,400 --> 00:34:12,710
It cost us our future.

349
00:34:14,180 --> 00:34:16,220
If there's no future, then why are we here?

350
00:34:16,220 --> 00:34:18,380
Why did you allow me to come?

351
00:34:18,670 --> 00:34:21,240
Not to help my enemies collaborate in my destruction.

352
00:34:21,240 --> 00:34:22,990
Yes, no, not what you hoped for,

353
00:34:22,990 --> 00:34:25,220
but you must have hoped for something.

354
00:34:26,630 --> 00:34:27,970
What did you hope for?

355
00:34:29,380 --> 00:34:32,900
- To make Jon Snow submit to your queen? - Mm, not like this.

356
00:34:32,900 --> 00:34:35,030
But eventually, you want everyone to bend the knee to her.

357
00:34:35,030 --> 00:34:36,170
- Yes. - Why?

358
00:34:38,040 --> 00:34:40,470
Because I think she will make the world a better place.

359
00:34:40,490 --> 00:34:42,280
You said she'd destroy King's Landing.

360
00:34:44,510 --> 00:34:45,740
She knows herself.

361
00:34:46,600 --> 00:34:48,630
She chose an advisor who would check her worst impulses

362
00:34:48,630 --> 00:34:50,970
instead of feeding them.

363
00:34:51,270 --> 00:34:53,120
That's the difference between you.

364
00:34:53,300 --> 00:34:55,400
I don't care about checking my worst impulses.

365
00:34:55,400 --> 00:34:57,940
I don't care about making the world a better place.

366
00:34:57,940 --> 00:34:58,980
Hang the world.

367
00:35:00,700 --> 00:35:02,540
That thing you dragged here,

368
00:35:02,910 --> 00:35:05,050
I know what it is, I know what it means.

369
00:35:06,010 --> 00:35:07,860
And when it came at me, I didn't think about the world.

370
00:35:07,860 --> 00:35:08,760
Not at all.

371
00:35:10,240 --> 00:35:11,410
As soon as it opened its mouth,

372
00:35:11,410 --> 00:35:14,810
the world disappeared for me, right down its black throat.

373
00:35:15,420 --> 00:35:17,350
All I could think about was keeping those gnashing teeth

374
00:35:17,360 --> 00:35:18,950
away from the ones who matter most,

375
00:35:18,950 --> 00:35:20,300
away from my family.

376
00:35:20,950 --> 00:35:22,960
Maybe Euron Greyjoy had the right idea.

377
00:35:24,800 --> 00:35:27,130
Get on a boat, take those who matter--

378
00:35:27,130 --> 00:35:28,520
You're pregnant.

379
00:36:01,020 --> 00:36:03,430
No one is less happy about this than I am.

380
00:36:04,000 --> 00:36:04,780
I know.

381
00:36:07,740 --> 00:36:09,100
I respect what you did.

382
00:36:10,420 --> 00:36:12,610
Wish you hadn't done it, but I respect it.

383
00:36:23,370 --> 00:36:26,640
This place was the beginning of the end for my family.

384
00:36:33,050 --> 00:36:34,690
A dragon is not a slave.

385
00:36:37,920 --> 00:36:39,270
They were terrifying.

386
00:36:40,650 --> 00:36:41,890
Extraordinary.

387
00:36:43,310 --> 00:36:46,120
They filled people with wonder and awe,

388
00:36:46,530 --> 00:36:48,470
and we locked them in here.

389
00:36:50,210 --> 00:36:51,290
They wasted away.

390
00:36:52,860 --> 00:36:53,940
They grew small.

391
00:36:55,450 --> 00:36:57,170
And we grew small as well.

392
00:36:59,230 --> 00:37:01,740
We weren't extraordinary without them.

393
00:37:02,240 --> 00:37:03,830
We were just like everyone else.

394
00:37:08,550 --> 00:37:10,230
You're not like everyone else.

395
00:37:16,440 --> 00:37:18,450
And your family hasn't seen its end.

396
00:37:20,040 --> 00:37:21,150
You're still here.

397
00:37:22,630 --> 00:37:24,030
I can't have children.

398
00:37:24,560 --> 00:37:25,730
Who told you that?

399
00:37:25,990 --> 00:37:27,640
The witch who murdered my husband.

400
00:37:28,950 --> 00:37:30,730
Has it occurred to you she might not have been

401
00:37:30,730 --> 00:37:33,020
a reliable source of information?

402
00:37:38,540 --> 00:37:40,000
You were right from the beginning.

403
00:37:41,210 --> 00:37:43,420
If I had trusted you, everything would be different.

404
00:37:47,790 --> 00:37:48,810
So, what now?

405
00:37:53,360 --> 00:37:55,620
I can't forget what I saw north of the Wall.

406
00:37:56,190 --> 00:37:57,560
And I can't pretend that Cersei

407
00:37:57,570 --> 00:38:01,220
won't take back half the country the moment I march north.

408
00:38:03,260 --> 00:38:05,500
It appears Tyrion's assessment was correct.

409
00:38:08,280 --> 00:38:09,490
We're fucked.

410
00:39:02,350 --> 00:39:04,030
My armies will not stand down.

411
00:39:06,000 --> 00:39:07,960
I will not pull them back to the capital.

412
00:39:11,720 --> 00:39:14,810
I will march them north to fight alongside you in the Great War.

413
00:39:17,210 --> 00:39:19,140
The darkness is coming for us all.

414
00:39:21,280 --> 00:39:22,510
We'll face it together.

415
00:39:24,190 --> 00:39:25,990
And when the Great War is over,

416
00:39:26,910 --> 00:39:29,270
perhaps you'll remember I chose to help

417
00:39:30,430 --> 00:39:33,540
with no promises or assurances from any of you.

418
00:39:37,210 --> 00:39:38,610
I expect not.

419
00:39:41,320 --> 00:39:42,510
Call our banners.

420
00:39:43,260 --> 00:39:44,120
All of them.

421
00:39:57,810 --> 00:40:00,550
It's not easy for ravens to fly in these storms.

422
00:40:01,210 --> 00:40:03,080
Perhaps Jon tried to send word earlier.

423
00:40:03,080 --> 00:40:06,320
No, this is the way he is,

424
00:40:06,320 --> 00:40:07,870
the way he's always been.

425
00:40:09,110 --> 00:40:11,520
He never asked for my opinion. Why would he start now?

426
00:40:11,720 --> 00:40:13,960
I can't believe he'd surrender the Northern crown

427
00:40:13,960 --> 00:40:15,040
without consulting you.

428
00:40:15,040 --> 00:40:17,640
This is his writing, his signature.

429
00:40:17,640 --> 00:40:20,450
He pledged to fight for Daenerys Targaryen.

430
00:40:20,820 --> 00:40:21,970
He's bent the knee.

431
00:40:22,660 --> 00:40:23,940
I've heard gossip

432
00:40:26,240 --> 00:40:29,650
that the Dragon Queen is quite beautiful.

433
00:40:29,760 --> 00:40:31,510
What does that have to do with anything?

434
00:40:33,850 --> 00:40:35,910
Jon is young and unmarried.

435
00:40:36,810 --> 00:40:38,870
Daenerys is young and unmarried.

436
00:40:39,810 --> 00:40:41,680
You think he wants to marry her?

437
00:40:42,450 --> 00:40:44,020
An alliance makes sense.

438
00:40:45,230 --> 00:40:47,010
Together, they'd be difficult to defeat.

439
00:40:49,020 --> 00:40:51,390
He was named King in the North.

440
00:40:54,250 --> 00:40:55,730
He can be unnamed.

441
00:40:59,470 --> 00:41:02,310
Even if I wanted to, Arya would never go along.

442
00:41:02,480 --> 00:41:05,120
She always loved Jon far more than she ever loved me,

443
00:41:05,120 --> 00:41:08,120
and she'd kill anyone who betrayed her family.

444
00:41:08,350 --> 00:41:09,680
You are family, too.

445
00:41:12,230 --> 00:41:14,420
Would Arya really murder her own sister?

446
00:41:15,500 --> 00:41:17,060
Do you know what she is now?

447
00:41:17,560 --> 00:41:19,610
Do you know what the Faceless Men are?

448
00:41:20,520 --> 00:41:21,930
Only by reputation.

449
00:41:23,300 --> 00:41:25,730
They worship the God of Death, I believe.

450
00:41:26,780 --> 00:41:28,430
I never trust godly men.

451
00:41:28,430 --> 00:41:29,520
They're killers.

452
00:41:30,180 --> 00:41:31,970
And Arya was one of them.

453
00:41:36,810 --> 00:41:38,220
What do you think she's after?

454
00:41:38,240 --> 00:41:39,440
She's your sister.

455
00:41:41,070 --> 00:41:43,220
You know her far better than I ever could.

456
00:41:46,640 --> 00:41:50,260
Sometimes when I try to understand a person's motives,

457
00:41:51,390 --> 00:41:52,600
I play a little game.

458
00:41:55,790 --> 00:41:57,310
I assume the worst.

459
00:42:00,830 --> 00:42:03,750
What's the worst reason they could possibly have

460
00:42:03,750 --> 00:42:07,260
for saying what they say and doing what they do?

461
00:42:08,770 --> 00:42:10,070
Then I ask myself,

462
00:42:10,840 --> 00:42:13,310
"How well does that reason explain

463
00:42:13,920 --> 00:42:16,850
what they say and what they do?"

464
00:42:18,860 --> 00:42:19,810
So, tell me--

465
00:42:20,900 --> 00:42:23,040
what's the worst thing she could want?

466
00:42:27,630 --> 00:42:29,090
She could want me dead

467
00:42:30,830 --> 00:42:33,060
because she thinks I wronged my family.

468
00:42:34,520 --> 00:42:36,130
Why did she come to Winterfell?

469
00:42:39,250 --> 00:42:40,330
To kill me

470
00:42:41,930 --> 00:42:45,060
for marrying our enemies and betraying my family.

471
00:42:45,290 --> 00:42:48,400
Why did she unearth the letter Cersei made you write?

472
00:42:50,840 --> 00:42:53,450
To provide proof of my betrayals.

473
00:42:55,110 --> 00:42:58,900
To provide justification after she murders me.

474
00:42:59,730 --> 00:43:02,460
And after she murders you,

475
00:43:03,920 --> 00:43:05,390
what does she become?

476
00:43:11,400 --> 00:43:12,800
Lady of Winterfell.

477
00:43:28,300 --> 00:43:31,320
If we have the Dothraki ride hard on the kingsroad,

478
00:43:31,410 --> 00:43:33,710
they'll arrive at Winterfell within the fortnight.

479
00:43:33,710 --> 00:43:34,990
And the Unsullied?

480
00:43:35,290 --> 00:43:36,830
We can sail with them to White Harbor,

481
00:43:36,830 --> 00:43:39,450
meet the Dothraki here on the kingsroad,

482
00:43:39,680 --> 00:43:41,800
then ride together to Winterfell.

483
00:43:42,850 --> 00:43:45,630
Perhaps you should fly to Winterfell, Your Grace.

484
00:43:46,000 --> 00:43:47,880
You have many enemies in the North.

485
00:43:48,160 --> 00:43:50,420
Thousands fell fighting your father.

486
00:43:50,780 --> 00:43:53,950
All it takes is one angry man with a crossbow.

487
00:43:54,460 --> 00:43:56,510
He'll see your silver hair on the kingsroad

488
00:43:56,520 --> 00:43:59,610
and know that one well-placed bolt will make him a hero.

489
00:44:00,330 --> 00:44:02,320
The man who killed the conqueror.

490
00:44:03,550 --> 00:44:05,240
It's your decision, Your Grace.

491
00:44:05,770 --> 00:44:08,130
But if we're going to be allies in this war,

492
00:44:08,840 --> 00:44:12,090
it's important for the Northerners to see us as allies.

493
00:44:13,000 --> 00:44:15,220
If we sail to White Harbor together,

494
00:44:16,110 --> 00:44:17,850
I think it sends a better message.

495
00:44:25,290 --> 00:44:27,100
I've not come to conquer the North.

496
00:44:27,970 --> 00:44:29,720
I'm coming to save the North.

497
00:44:35,440 --> 00:44:36,480
We sail together.

498
00:44:51,900 --> 00:44:52,650
Jon.

499
00:44:55,280 --> 00:44:56,410
Can I speak with you?

500
00:44:59,810 --> 00:45:00,570
All right.

501
00:45:06,810 --> 00:45:08,270
What you did in King's Landing,

502
00:45:10,140 --> 00:45:11,130
what you said...

503
00:45:13,650 --> 00:45:16,780
you could've lied to Cersei

504
00:45:17,930 --> 00:45:20,070
about bending the knee to Daenerys.

505
00:45:24,110 --> 00:45:26,300
You risked everything to tell an enemy the truth.

506
00:45:28,330 --> 00:45:30,350
We went down there to make peace.

507
00:45:30,930 --> 00:45:34,180
And it seems to me we need to be honest with each other

508
00:45:34,180 --> 00:45:35,780
if we're going to fight together.

509
00:45:37,430 --> 00:45:39,190
You've always known what was right.

510
00:45:43,330 --> 00:45:45,720
Even when we were all young and stupid,

511
00:45:46,550 --> 00:45:47,670
you always knew.

512
00:45:48,660 --> 00:45:50,190
Every step you take...

513
00:45:51,810 --> 00:45:53,390
it's always the right step.

514
00:45:53,390 --> 00:45:54,580
It's not.

515
00:45:54,790 --> 00:45:56,950
It may seem that way from the outside,

516
00:45:56,950 --> 00:46:00,510
but I promise you, it's not true.

517
00:46:03,050 --> 00:46:05,490
I've done plenty of things that I regret.

518
00:46:05,490 --> 00:46:07,290
Not compared to me, you haven't.

519
00:46:07,520 --> 00:46:08,320
No.

520
00:46:10,780 --> 00:46:12,200
Not compared to you.

521
00:46:23,580 --> 00:46:25,810
I always wanted to do the right thing.

522
00:46:28,890 --> 00:46:30,820
Be the right kind of person.

523
00:46:31,530 --> 00:46:33,320
But I never knew what that meant.

524
00:46:35,170 --> 00:46:37,070
It always seemed like there's...

525
00:46:41,480 --> 00:46:44,110
like there was an impossible choice I had to make.

526
00:46:46,270 --> 00:46:47,930
Stark or Greyjoy.

527
00:46:51,450 --> 00:46:55,710
Our father was more of a father to you than yours ever was.

528
00:46:55,710 --> 00:46:57,840
- He was. - And you betrayed him.

529
00:46:58,780 --> 00:47:00,500
Betrayed his memory.

530
00:47:00,770 --> 00:47:01,620
I did.

531
00:47:06,670 --> 00:47:07,990
But you never lost him.

532
00:47:12,240 --> 00:47:13,590
He's a part of you.

533
00:47:15,880 --> 00:47:17,670
Just like he's a part of me.

534
00:47:18,090 --> 00:47:19,650
But the things I've done...

535
00:47:21,510 --> 00:47:23,800
It's not my place to forgive you for all of it.

536
00:47:27,800 --> 00:47:29,450
But what I can forgive,

537
00:47:30,830 --> 00:47:31,660
I do.

538
00:47:38,660 --> 00:47:40,230
You don't need to choose.

539
00:47:42,150 --> 00:47:43,560
You're a Greyjoy...

540
00:47:46,330 --> 00:47:47,710
and you're a Stark.

541
00:48:01,250 --> 00:48:02,910
When I was Ramsay's prisoner,

542
00:48:04,330 --> 00:48:07,450
Yara tried to save me.

543
00:48:09,470 --> 00:48:10,760
She's the only one

544
00:48:11,840 --> 00:48:13,230
who tried to save me.

545
00:48:20,800 --> 00:48:21,960
She needs me now.

546
00:48:23,680 --> 00:48:25,450
So, why are you still talking to me?

547
00:48:39,850 --> 00:48:40,770
Load up.

548
00:48:41,010 --> 00:48:42,670
Load up, lads. Go on.

549
00:48:43,370 --> 00:48:44,650
Tide's coming in.

550
00:49:01,620 --> 00:49:04,070
All of us chose to follow Yara.

551
00:49:06,790 --> 00:49:09,260
We left the Iron Islands for Yara.

552
00:49:10,840 --> 00:49:12,780
She would never leave one of us behind.

553
00:49:16,370 --> 00:49:17,830
We're not leaving her behind.

554
00:49:17,830 --> 00:49:19,150
Your sister's dead.

555
00:49:19,150 --> 00:49:20,980
- She's not dead. - She's dead.

556
00:49:21,120 --> 00:49:24,030
Even if Euron hasn't cut her throat yet, she's dead.

557
00:49:24,030 --> 00:49:25,210
She's our queen.

558
00:49:25,210 --> 00:49:28,620
She's your sister, and you left her to die.

559
00:49:29,210 --> 00:49:30,030
I did.

560
00:49:33,050 --> 00:49:34,720
I ran from my uncle.

561
00:49:36,140 --> 00:49:37,280
I was a coward.

562
00:49:37,280 --> 00:49:40,420
So, why in fuck's name should we listen to you?

563
00:49:40,840 --> 00:49:43,070
They say the dead can't swim.

564
00:49:44,210 --> 00:49:45,720
We're going to sail east,

565
00:49:45,870 --> 00:49:47,840
find a nice, quiet island,

566
00:49:48,070 --> 00:49:51,220
kill all the men, and take their wives for ourselves.

567
00:49:51,230 --> 00:49:53,460
- We're done with all that. - Who says we are?

568
00:49:53,460 --> 00:49:56,320
Yara did. She made a pledge.

569
00:49:58,530 --> 00:49:59,930
We're going to find her,

570
00:50:01,690 --> 00:50:03,160
and we're going to set her free.

571
00:50:13,080 --> 00:50:14,890
Run away, little Theon.

572
00:50:15,920 --> 00:50:17,440
It's what you do best.

573
00:50:20,720 --> 00:50:22,110
He needs to shut his mouth.

574
00:50:36,460 --> 00:50:37,270
yes!

575
00:50:38,780 --> 00:50:40,450
That's more like it.

576
00:50:58,140 --> 00:50:59,280
Stay down...

577
00:51:00,210 --> 00:51:01,660
or I'll kill you!

578
00:51:12,620 --> 00:51:15,990
I said stay down or I'll kill you!

579
00:52:28,940 --> 00:52:30,070
Not for me.

580
00:52:33,980 --> 00:52:35,050
For Yara!

581
00:52:35,420 --> 00:52:36,960
Yara!

582
00:53:22,220 --> 00:53:24,530
Have my sister brought to the Great Hall.

583
00:54:10,350 --> 00:54:12,130
Are you sure you want to do this?

584
00:54:14,960 --> 00:54:17,780
It's not what I want. It's what honor demands.

585
00:54:19,110 --> 00:54:20,750
And what does honor demand?

586
00:54:21,070 --> 00:54:24,250
That I defend my family from those who would harm us.

587
00:54:24,600 --> 00:54:27,300
That I defend the North from those who would betray us.

588
00:54:29,900 --> 00:54:30,790
All right, then.

589
00:54:33,000 --> 00:54:34,020
Get on with it.

590
00:54:37,090 --> 00:54:39,190
You stand accused of murder.

591
00:54:39,670 --> 00:54:41,490
You stand accused of treason.

592
00:54:42,540 --> 00:54:44,440
How do you answer these charges...

593
00:54:47,480 --> 00:54:48,820
Lord Baelish?

594
00:55:04,950 --> 00:55:06,610
My sister asked you a question.

595
00:55:11,240 --> 00:55:12,760
Lady Sansa, forgive me...

596
00:55:14,580 --> 00:55:16,050
I'm a bit confused.

597
00:55:16,050 --> 00:55:18,060
Which charges confuse you?

598
00:55:18,480 --> 00:55:20,190
Let's start with the simplest one.

599
00:55:20,590 --> 00:55:23,270
you murdered our aunt, Lysa Arryn.

600
00:55:23,300 --> 00:55:25,660
You pushed her through the Moon Door and watched her fall.

601
00:55:25,660 --> 00:55:27,030
Do you deny it?

602
00:55:29,770 --> 00:55:31,190
I did it to protect you.

603
00:55:31,190 --> 00:55:33,290
You did it to take power in the Vale.

604
00:55:33,850 --> 00:55:36,610
Earlier, you conspired to murder Jon Arryn.

605
00:55:36,610 --> 00:55:38,940
You gave Lysa Tears of Lys to poison him.

606
00:55:38,940 --> 00:55:40,260
Do you deny it?

607
00:55:42,520 --> 00:55:44,530
Whatever your aunt might have told you...

608
00:55:46,060 --> 00:55:47,570
she was a troubled woman.

609
00:55:48,920 --> 00:55:50,260
She imagined enemies everywhere.

610
00:55:50,260 --> 00:55:53,040
You had Aunt Lysa send a letter to our parents

611
00:55:53,040 --> 00:55:55,420
telling them it was the Lannisters who murdered Jon Arryn

612
00:55:55,420 --> 00:55:56,860
when, really, it was you.

613
00:55:56,860 --> 00:55:59,220
The conflict between the Starks and the Lannisters,

614
00:55:59,220 --> 00:56:00,650
it was you who started it.

615
00:56:00,650 --> 00:56:01,780
Do you deny it?

616
00:56:01,780 --> 00:56:03,030
I know of no such letter.

617
00:56:03,030 --> 00:56:06,280
You conspired with Cersei Lannister and Joffrey Baratheon

618
00:56:06,280 --> 00:56:09,070
to betray our father, Ned Stark.

619
00:56:09,070 --> 00:56:11,800
Thanks to your treachery, he was imprisoned

620
00:56:11,800 --> 00:56:15,110
and later executed on false charges of treason.

621
00:56:15,110 --> 00:56:17,840
- Do you deny it? - I deny it!

622
00:56:18,690 --> 00:56:21,330
None of you were there to see what happened.

623
00:56:21,400 --> 00:56:23,000
None of you knows the truth.

624
00:56:23,100 --> 00:56:24,790
You held a knife to his throat.

625
00:56:30,250 --> 00:56:32,790
You said, "I did warn you not the trust me."

626
00:56:36,420 --> 00:56:40,230
You told our mother this knife belonged to Tyrion Lannister.

627
00:56:42,190 --> 00:56:43,910
But that was another one of your lies.

628
00:56:44,570 --> 00:56:45,640
It was yours.

629
00:56:51,480 --> 00:56:54,200
Lady Sansa, I have known you since you were a girl.

630
00:56:54,200 --> 00:56:56,440
- I've protected you. - Protected me?

631
00:56:56,880 --> 00:56:59,010
By selling me to the Boltons?

632
00:57:00,070 --> 00:57:01,480
If we could speak alone,

633
00:57:02,500 --> 00:57:04,020
I can explain everything.

634
00:57:06,390 --> 00:57:09,180
Sometimes when I'm trying to understand a person's motives,

635
00:57:09,190 --> 00:57:10,760
I play a little game.

636
00:57:11,940 --> 00:57:13,330
I assume the worst.

637
00:57:15,210 --> 00:57:16,650
What's the worst reason you have

638
00:57:16,650 --> 00:57:18,690
for turning me against my sister?

639
00:57:20,700 --> 00:57:22,590
That's what you do, isn't it?

640
00:57:22,590 --> 00:57:24,380
That's what you've always done--

641
00:57:24,380 --> 00:57:26,150
turn family against family,

642
00:57:26,150 --> 00:57:28,130
turn sister against sister.

643
00:57:28,130 --> 00:57:30,510
That's what you did to our mother and Aunt Lysa,

644
00:57:30,510 --> 00:57:32,560
and that's what you tried to do to us.

645
00:57:32,560 --> 00:57:33,960
Sansa, please.

646
00:57:33,990 --> 00:57:36,800
I'm a slow learner, it's true.

647
00:57:38,260 --> 00:57:39,090
But I learn.

648
00:57:39,090 --> 00:57:41,070
Give me a chance to defend myself.

649
00:57:41,800 --> 00:57:42,980
I deserve that.

650
00:57:48,740 --> 00:57:49,920
I am Lord Protector of the Vale

651
00:57:49,920 --> 00:57:52,510
and I command you to escort me safely back to the Eyrie.

652
00:57:52,510 --> 00:57:53,890
I think not.

653
00:57:57,080 --> 00:57:59,730
Sansa, I beg you!

654
00:58:01,490 --> 00:58:03,260
I loved your mother since the time I was a boy.

655
00:58:03,260 --> 00:58:05,210
And yet, you betrayed her.

656
00:58:07,170 --> 00:58:08,260
I loved you.

657
00:58:10,560 --> 00:58:11,720
More than anyone.

658
00:58:13,160 --> 00:58:15,120
And yet, you betrayed me.

659
00:58:17,570 --> 00:58:19,330
When you brought me back to Winterfell,

660
00:58:19,330 --> 00:58:21,710
you told me there's no justice in the world,

661
00:58:21,710 --> 00:58:23,630
not unless we make it.

662
00:58:26,160 --> 00:58:29,060
Thank you for all your many lessons, Lord Baelish.

663
00:58:30,740 --> 00:58:32,080
I will never forget them.

664
00:58:36,290 --> 00:58:37,210
Sansa!

665
00:58:44,480 --> 00:58:45,310
I...

666
00:59:08,880 --> 00:59:09,920
Our men in King's Landing

667
00:59:09,920 --> 00:59:11,730
will march north in three days' time.

668
00:59:11,810 --> 00:59:12,860
It'll take us a fortnight

669
00:59:12,860 --> 00:59:14,650
just to gather supplies for the train.

670
00:59:14,650 --> 00:59:15,900
We don't have a fortnight.

671
00:59:15,940 --> 00:59:17,920
If the North falls, we fall. Three days.

672
00:59:17,920 --> 00:59:19,370
The remaining forces in the Westerlands

673
00:59:19,370 --> 00:59:21,110
will take the river road east.

674
00:59:21,280 --> 00:59:22,520
We'll meet at Lord Harroway's Town

675
00:59:22,530 --> 00:59:24,700
and march together to Winterfell.

676
00:59:24,780 --> 00:59:25,800
Ser Jaime.

677
00:59:26,820 --> 00:59:27,780
Your Grace.

678
00:59:28,740 --> 00:59:30,770
My lords, I need a moment with my brother.

679
00:59:32,710 --> 00:59:33,680
Your Grace.

680
00:59:37,820 --> 00:59:41,450
- What are you doing? - Preparing the expedition north.

681
00:59:41,450 --> 00:59:42,810
Expedition north?

682
00:59:44,040 --> 00:59:46,480
I always knew you were the stupidest Lannister.

683
00:59:47,500 --> 00:59:49,850
The Starks and Targaryens have united against us,

684
00:59:49,850 --> 00:59:51,990
and you want to fight alongside them?

685
00:59:51,990 --> 00:59:54,000
Are you a traitor or an idiot?

686
00:59:54,000 --> 00:59:55,850
You pledged our forces to fight our common enemy--

687
00:59:55,850 --> 00:59:57,390
I'll say whatever I need to say

688
00:59:57,390 --> 00:59:59,330
to ensure the survival of our house.

689
00:59:59,400 --> 01:00:02,010
You expect me to trust the man who murdered our father?

690
01:00:02,020 --> 01:00:05,330
You expect me to command our troops to fight beside foreign scum,

691
01:00:05,640 --> 01:00:07,250
to fight for the Dragon Queen?

692
01:00:07,260 --> 01:00:08,860
You saw it with your own eyes.

693
01:00:08,860 --> 01:00:10,900
You saw a dead man trying to kill us.

694
01:00:10,910 --> 01:00:12,610
And I saw it burn.

695
01:00:13,000 --> 01:00:14,980
If dragons can't stop them,

696
01:00:14,980 --> 01:00:18,100
if Dothraki and Unsullied and Northmen can't stop them,

697
01:00:18,100 --> 01:00:19,980
how will our armies make a difference?

698
01:00:19,980 --> 01:00:22,020
This isn't about noble houses,

699
01:00:22,020 --> 01:00:24,270
this is about the living and the dead!

700
01:00:24,270 --> 01:00:26,420
And I intend to stay amongst the living.

701
01:00:26,810 --> 01:00:29,680
Let the Stark boy and his new queen defend the North.

702
01:00:29,830 --> 01:00:31,670
We stay here where we've always been.

703
01:00:31,670 --> 01:00:33,620
I made a promise.

704
01:00:36,460 --> 01:00:39,820
Our child will rule Westeros.

705
01:00:39,820 --> 01:00:44,260
Our child will never be born if the dead come south.

706
01:00:44,610 --> 01:00:46,040
The monsters are real.

707
01:00:47,110 --> 01:00:48,250
The white walkers,

708
01:00:48,250 --> 01:00:51,050
the dragons, the Dothraki screamers--

709
01:00:51,130 --> 01:00:52,160
all the frightening stories

710
01:00:52,160 --> 01:00:54,180
we heard when we were young, they're all real.

711
01:00:54,180 --> 01:00:55,320
So be it.

712
01:00:56,250 --> 01:00:58,090
Let the monsters kill each other.

713
01:00:58,620 --> 01:01:00,480
And while they battle in the North,

714
01:01:00,970 --> 01:01:03,010
we take back the lands that belong to us.

715
01:01:03,010 --> 01:01:05,880
- And then what? - And then we rule.

716
01:01:06,120 --> 01:01:08,540
When the fighting in the North is over, someone wins.

717
01:01:08,540 --> 01:01:10,490
You understand that, don't you?

718
01:01:11,090 --> 01:01:14,850
If the dead win, they march south and kill us all.

719
01:01:14,980 --> 01:01:17,540
If the living win, and we've betrayed them,

720
01:01:17,540 --> 01:01:19,750
they march south and kill us all!

721
01:01:19,750 --> 01:01:22,610
The Targaryens and the Starks already want to kill us all.

722
01:01:22,620 --> 01:01:23,830
Most of them will die in the North.

723
01:01:23,840 --> 01:01:25,540
I faced them in the field.

724
01:01:25,550 --> 01:01:27,690
We can't beat them. We can't beat their dragons.

725
01:01:27,700 --> 01:01:29,570
How many dragons did you see at the pit?

726
01:01:29,570 --> 01:01:31,430
- Two. - What happened to the third?

727
01:01:31,550 --> 01:01:33,670
For all we know, it's guarding her fleet!

728
01:01:34,450 --> 01:01:35,680
She came here with her dragons

729
01:01:35,680 --> 01:01:37,340
and her Dothraki and her Unsullied.

730
01:01:37,340 --> 01:01:39,320
She came here to show us all her power.

731
01:01:40,280 --> 01:01:43,380
No, something happened. The dragons are vulnerable.

732
01:01:43,380 --> 01:01:45,840
We can't beat the Dothraki. We don't have the numbers.

733
01:01:45,850 --> 01:01:47,700
We don't have the support of the other houses!

734
01:01:47,700 --> 01:01:50,450
No, we have something better. We have the Iron Bank.

735
01:01:52,510 --> 01:01:53,300
You should've listened more

736
01:01:53,300 --> 01:01:56,180
when Father spoke about the importance of gold.

737
01:01:56,260 --> 01:01:58,050
Oh, I know it's boring for you.

738
01:01:58,470 --> 01:02:01,330
You just wanted to hunt and ride and fight.

739
01:02:02,000 --> 01:02:03,750
But I listened, I learned.

740
01:02:05,020 --> 01:02:08,310
Highgarden bought us the most powerful army in Essos--

741
01:02:08,660 --> 01:02:10,110
the Golden Company.

742
01:02:10,510 --> 01:02:14,130
20,000 men, horses, elephants, I believe.

743
01:02:14,130 --> 01:02:15,930
The Golden Company is not here.

744
01:02:15,930 --> 01:02:17,090
They're in Essos.

745
01:02:17,260 --> 01:02:21,190
How is a mercenary company in Essos going to help us?

746
01:02:21,190 --> 01:02:23,530
Do you really think Euron Greyjoy turned tail

747
01:02:23,530 --> 01:02:25,570
and sailed back to the Iron Islands?

748
01:02:26,810 --> 01:02:29,580
Do you think he abandoned the chance to marry the queen?

749
01:02:31,150 --> 01:02:32,810
No one walks away from me.

750
01:02:35,290 --> 01:02:36,760
He's sailing with his fleet to Essos.

751
01:02:36,760 --> 01:02:38,900
He's going to ferry the Golden Company back here

752
01:02:38,900 --> 01:02:41,050
to help us win the war for Westeros.

753
01:02:43,060 --> 01:02:46,070
You plotted with Euron Greyjoy without telling me,

754
01:02:46,070 --> 01:02:48,270
the commander of your armies?

755
01:02:48,570 --> 01:02:50,340
And you conspired with Tyrion,

756
01:02:50,690 --> 01:02:51,830
the man who murdered our father,

757
01:02:51,830 --> 01:02:53,100
without telling me, your queen.

758
01:02:53,100 --> 01:02:54,280
I didn't conspire with him.

759
01:02:54,280 --> 01:02:56,630
You met with him in secret without my consent.

760
01:02:56,630 --> 01:02:58,700
You planned to promote my enemies' interests.

761
01:02:58,700 --> 01:03:00,960
That is the definition of conspiracy.

762
01:03:00,960 --> 01:03:03,240
I pledged to ride north.

763
01:03:03,340 --> 01:03:05,400
I intend to honor that pledge.

764
01:03:05,410 --> 01:03:07,340
- And that will be treason. - Treason?

765
01:03:07,340 --> 01:03:09,620
Disobeying your queen's command, fighting with her enemies.

766
01:03:09,620 --> 01:03:11,270
What would you call it?

767
01:03:12,970 --> 01:03:15,140
Doesn't matter what I'd call it.

768
01:03:21,790 --> 01:03:24,190
I told you no one walks away from me.

769
01:03:26,940 --> 01:03:28,800
Are you going to order him to kill me?

770
01:03:31,600 --> 01:03:33,620
I'm the only one you have left.

771
01:03:33,690 --> 01:03:35,940
Our children are gone, our father is gone.

772
01:03:35,950 --> 01:03:37,780
It's just me and you now.

773
01:03:38,080 --> 01:03:39,670
There's one more yet to come.

774
01:03:42,780 --> 01:03:43,920
Give the order, then.

775
01:04:04,120 --> 01:04:05,530
I don't believe you.

776
01:05:54,900 --> 01:05:55,590
Come in.

777
01:06:00,200 --> 01:06:01,470
Samwell Tarly.

778
01:06:01,990 --> 01:06:03,830
I wasn't sure if you'd remember me.

779
01:06:04,180 --> 01:06:05,520
I remember everything.

780
01:06:13,900 --> 01:06:15,620
You helped us get beyond the Wall.

781
01:06:16,050 --> 01:06:18,350
- You're a good man. - Oh, well, thank you,

782
01:06:18,350 --> 01:06:21,410
but, um, I'm not sure that I am.

783
01:06:25,500 --> 01:06:27,200
What happened to you beyond the Wall?

784
01:06:28,900 --> 01:06:30,690
I became the Three-Eyed Raven.

785
01:06:36,540 --> 01:06:37,950
I don't know what that means.

786
01:06:39,040 --> 01:06:41,410
I can see things that happened in the past.

787
01:06:42,710 --> 01:06:44,630
I can see things happening now

788
01:06:45,650 --> 01:06:46,840
all over the world.

789
01:06:49,140 --> 01:06:50,910
Why did you come to Winterfell?

790
01:06:56,160 --> 01:06:57,990
Jon's the one to lead the fight against the dead.

791
01:06:57,990 --> 01:06:59,170
I know he is.

792
01:07:00,120 --> 01:07:01,650
But he can't do it alone,

793
01:07:02,280 --> 01:07:04,550
so I've come here to help him.

794
01:07:05,390 --> 01:07:07,250
He's on his way back to Winterfell

795
01:07:07,860 --> 01:07:09,630
with Daenerys Targaryen.

796
01:07:10,750 --> 01:07:13,430
You-- you saw this in--

797
01:07:13,890 --> 01:07:14,990
in a vision?

798
01:07:22,380 --> 01:07:24,370
He needs to know the truth.

799
01:07:25,910 --> 01:07:27,110
The truth about what?

800
01:07:27,110 --> 01:07:28,630
About himself.

801
01:07:28,930 --> 01:07:31,350
No one knows. No one but me.

802
01:07:32,550 --> 01:07:34,720
Jon isn't really my father's son.

803
01:07:35,660 --> 01:07:37,470
He's the son of Rhaegar Targaryen

804
01:07:37,470 --> 01:07:39,850
and my aunt, Lyanna Stark.

805
01:07:40,520 --> 01:07:42,690
He was born in a tower in Dorne.

806
01:07:43,330 --> 01:07:45,410
His last name isn't really Snow,

807
01:07:45,780 --> 01:07:47,010
it's Sand.

808
01:07:49,470 --> 01:07:50,470
It's not.

809
01:07:51,880 --> 01:07:54,050
Dornish bastards are named Sand.

810
01:07:54,260 --> 01:07:57,600
At the Citadel, I transcribed a High Septon's diary.

811
01:07:58,760 --> 01:08:00,980
He annulled Rhaegar's marriage to Elia.

812
01:08:02,830 --> 01:08:05,580
He wed Rhaegar and Lyanna in a secret ceremony.

813
01:08:06,700 --> 01:08:07,960
Are you certain?

814
01:08:07,960 --> 01:08:10,690
It's what the High Septon wrote in his private diary.

815
01:08:10,880 --> 01:08:12,430
I don't know why he'd lie.

816
01:08:14,570 --> 01:08:16,230
Is this something you can see?

817
01:08:18,910 --> 01:08:22,100
Father, Smith, Warrior,

818
01:08:22,610 --> 01:08:27,140
Mother, Maiden, Crone, Stranger.

819
01:08:27,400 --> 01:08:30,520
- I am hers and she is mine... - I am his and he is mine...

820
01:08:31,070 --> 01:08:35,010
from this day until the end of my days.

821
01:08:36,060 --> 01:08:38,280
Robert's Rebellion was built on a lie.

822
01:08:40,540 --> 01:08:43,570
Rhaegar didn't kidnap my aunt or rape her.

823
01:08:53,220 --> 01:08:54,220
He loved her.

824
01:09:02,700 --> 01:09:03,750
And she loved him.

825
01:09:30,740 --> 01:09:31,680
And Jon...

826
01:09:35,660 --> 01:09:37,170
Jon's real name...

827
01:09:39,450 --> 01:09:43,080
His name is Aegon Targaryen.

828
01:09:44,060 --> 01:09:45,790
You have to protect him.

829
01:09:47,510 --> 01:09:48,890
Promise me, Ned.

830
01:10:12,150 --> 01:10:14,040
He's never been a bastard.

831
01:10:18,440 --> 01:10:20,460
He's the heir to the Iron Throne.

832
01:10:36,010 --> 01:10:37,120
He needs to know.

833
01:10:40,880 --> 01:10:42,030
We need to tell him.

834
01:10:53,040 --> 01:10:54,060
Are you all right?

835
01:10:55,760 --> 01:10:57,390
It's just strange.

836
01:10:58,350 --> 01:11:01,370
In his own horrible way, I believe he loved me.

837
01:11:05,720 --> 01:11:06,980
You did the right thing.

838
01:11:07,010 --> 01:11:08,230
You did it.

839
01:11:09,530 --> 01:11:11,190
I'm just the executioner.

840
01:11:11,600 --> 01:11:13,170
You passed the sentence.

841
01:11:15,600 --> 01:11:17,130
You're the Lady of Winterfell.

842
01:11:18,250 --> 01:11:19,500
Does that bother you?

843
01:11:22,390 --> 01:11:24,770
I was never going to be as good a lady as you.

844
01:11:26,450 --> 01:11:28,190
So I had to be something else.

845
01:11:30,350 --> 01:11:32,550
I never could have survived what you survived.

846
01:11:32,980 --> 01:11:34,020
You would have.

847
01:11:35,350 --> 01:11:37,180
You're the strongest person I know.

848
01:11:41,510 --> 01:11:44,110
I believe that's the nicest thing you've ever said to me.

849
01:11:45,450 --> 01:11:48,470
Well, don't get used to it.

850
01:11:49,320 --> 01:11:51,470
You're still very strange and annoying.

851
01:11:58,070 --> 01:12:00,240
"In winter, we must protect ourselves.

852
01:12:01,610 --> 01:12:03,060
Look after one another."

853
01:12:05,830 --> 01:12:06,840
Father.

854
01:12:10,690 --> 01:12:13,940
"When the snows fall and the white winds blow,

855
01:12:14,680 --> 01:12:16,510
the lone wolf dies,

856
01:12:16,930 --> 01:12:18,850
but the pack survives."

857
01:12:26,280 --> 01:12:27,220
I miss him.

858
01:12:30,760 --> 01:12:31,720
Me, too.

859
01:13:54,600 --> 01:13:56,010
It's a long way down.

860
01:13:56,110 --> 01:13:59,540
Yeah. The crows keep telling me I'll get used to it.

861
01:14:09,060 --> 01:14:11,450
I can see movement...

862
01:14:12,180 --> 01:14:14,040
Watch, on the tree line!

863
01:14:15,420 --> 01:14:16,440
What is it?

864
01:15:48,700 --> 01:15:49,480
Come on!

865
01:15:50,520 --> 01:15:52,810
Run! Run!

